{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy","id":1553010,"title":"The Euthanatos Tradition and the Sphere of Entropy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-08T08:51:29-07:00","id":1553010,"title":"The Euthanatos Tradition and the Sphere of Entropy","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hi there!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">(Please forgive my English, as it is not my native language.)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I have a hard time understanding the relation or link between the Euthanatos and Entropy.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">On one hand, the Tradition mages are the ones who sees if someone\u2019s life should be ended or if it should go on. How does one see this with the Entropy sphere? The tradition\u2019s description shows them mostly as \u201c death-mages \u201c (death, in a neutral sense, not a bad sense), where they kill someone who\u2019s time has come, or kill someone who disrupts the natural way / the Wheel.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">On the other hand, the Entropy Sphere is mainly about, fate, fortune, and luck. Sure, it is also about decay and weak spot. The sphere is mostly about affecting probabilities and decay. But where in the sphere description does it shows how to determine if someone\u2019s time has come (to die) or if someone\u2019s time has not yet come?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">With the Life sphere, you can see if someone is sick, and you can choose to heal him/her, or not.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">But in the Entropy sphere, in the description, I don\u2019t see how an Entropic mage can determine where someone\u2019s position is on the Wheel\u2026</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So, Story-wise and rule-wise, how does all of this is determined and how does it works?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">In mainly use the M20 edition, but I went and checked in the second edition and in the revised edition. And I still didn\u2019t find the answers I\u2019m looking.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Maybe it\u2019s obvious and I just didn\u2019t understand what\u2019s in front of me in the books, so I apologize in advance for asking this question.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Thanks in advance for your time and patience to all who will answer!</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25337-lightbringer1","name":"Lightbringer1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T09:45:16-07:00","id":1553011,"title":"","content":"Well, Entropy 1 can see wheter someone it's close to death. Just like you can sense danger. But that's not what Euthanatos mean when they say things like &quot;kill someone who\u2019s time has come&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's mostly a judgement call based on their own moral code, that I don't remember exactly, but can be roughly summarized as, so to speak: People that cause a lot of suffering and make the world worse are a waste of air and need to do better, send them back to the cycle to see if next time they do better. <br /> <br /> No Sphere can tell you &quot;when it's morally correct to kill someone&quot;. At most, you could do some research, and then convince yourself that whatever information you now have justifies your actions. <br /> <br /> Important note: While particularly evil humans may be up for the good death, this judgement it's often to mages that have accumulated too much death ressonance, and this is accumulated mostly by killing people with magick - so an Euthanatos that it's too eager to kill bad people with their power will end on the list as well. Killing it's understood as a last resort.<br /> <br /> But why Entropy?: It's the sphere of fate, and Euthanatos often see themselves as &quot;hands of fate&quot;, so it makes sense they would have powers bestowed to them by fate. It has ties to necromancy trough how the underworld and the concept of decay relates to magick (which it's a little contrived, but it's what it is), and Euthanatos come from people that tended the dead. In a Doylist sense, it's because of the whole &quot;heat death of the universe&quot; mythic that surrounds concept of entropy - ultimately entropy will bring the &quot;good death&quot; to the universe itself<br /> <br /> But, really, all the Spheres assignation to a given Tradition are a little arbitrary, hence why you can choose other Spheres to be your main on M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T12:17:10-07:00","id":1553012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lightbringer1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy#post1553010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I have a hard time understanding the relation or link between the Euthanatos and Entropy.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, it's a matter of understanding three concepts (I'll use the Hindu concepts instead of the in-game ones, because I think they're actually more didactic):<br /> <br /> 1- <b>Entropy</b> is also the Sphere of complex systems, their dynamics and evolution. This is, in the end, what unifies fate and decay as a single concept. For the <b><i>Euthanatoi</i></b>, the focus is to understand the Wheel as a system. While its purpose and goal is abstractly important, their focus is in its workings right now;<br /> <br /> 2- The key to understand what the <b><i>Euthanatoi</i></b> call The Wheel are the concepts of <i>Samsara</i> and <i>Moksha</i>. Basically they believe every incarnation has a personal purpose of being a means to learn and change, and eventually achieve Enlightenment. The Wheel is <i>Samsara</i>, the eternal cycle of reincarnation where everyone is constantly living, dying and coming back, slowly moving towards a Liberation from this unending cycle, which is <i>Moksha</i>;<br /> <br /> 3- Aside from the personal goal of attaining <i>Moksha</i>, every life has a role to fulfill for others and for the community, or <i>Dharma</i>. For the <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> this includes both current <i>Dharma</i> and the notion of fate, but not as in what will happen to you, and instead as in what good you'll bring in your future. So beyond the goal of achieving <i>Moksha</i>, you have a duty to help (consciously or not) other to do the same.<br /> <br /> Usually happiness has a strong role to play in all this, but it's not necessarily so. Most <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> will avoid to kill someone who is and/or will make others happy, but this isn't always the case.<br /> <br /> Once you get all those concepts, what the <i><b>Euthanaoi</b></i> understand is that the Wheel, <i>Samsara</i>, can become temporarily clogged. Sometimes people reach a point where, in their current life, they're neither advancing towards <i>Moksha</i>, nor helping anyone to do so, neither being happy or making others happy or helping community in any way. In some cases, they're actively hindering others in such a way that whatever good their lives are producing, it's not being worth it.<br /> <br /> So the <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> assume the role of unclogging <i>Samsara</i> by ending this life, so the person can reincarnate again and return to advancement. It can be a bad person that hinders others as well as themselves, but it can also be a patient so ill that continuing life will only bring pointless suffering to all involved, a person whose fate from now is to stop advancement, or any other number of things. The point is the <i><b>system</b></i> of <i>Samsara</i>, its health, so to speak, and if a person's life benefits it, or if cleaning the slate is a better course of action.<br /> <br /> Remember that in all cases, they believe in reincarnation. Actually eliminating the <i>Atma</i>, the real immortal soul, is possibly the most terrible sin, only to be carried if that soul's continued existence is truly anathema to everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T16:40:38-07:00","id":1553075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553012#post1553012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In addition to everything <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> said, it's a matter of understanding three concepts (I'll use the Hindu concepts instead of the in-game ones, because I think they're actually more didactic):<br /> <br /> 1- <b>Entropy</b> is also the Sphere of complex systems, their dynamics and evolution. This is, in the end, what unifies fate and decay as a single concept. For the <b><i>Euthanatoi</i></b>, the focus is to understand the Wheel as a system. While its purpose and goal is abstractly important, their focus is in its workings right now;<br /> <br /> 2- The key to understand what the <b><i>Euthanatoi</i></b> call The Wheel are the concepts of <i>Samsara</i> and <i>Moksha</i>. Basically they believe every incarnation has a personal purpose of being a means to learn and change, and eventually achieve Enlightenment. The Wheel is <i>Samsara</i>, the eternal cycle of reincarnation where everyone is constantly living, dying and coming back, slowly moving towards a Liberation from this unending cycle, which is <i>Moksha</i>;<br /> <br /> 3- Aside from the personal goal of attaining <i>Moksha</i>, every life has a role to fulfill for others and for the community, or <i>Dharma</i>. For the <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> this includes both current <i>Dharma</i> and the notion of fate, but not as in what will happen to you, and instead as in what good you'll bring in your future. So beyond the goal of achieving <i>Moksha</i>, you have a duty to help (consciously or not) other to do the same.<br /> <br /> Usually happiness has a strong role to play in all this, but it's not necessarily so. Most <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> will avoid to kill someone who is and/or will make others happy, but this isn't always the case.<br /> <br /> Once you get all those concepts, what the <i><b>Euthanaoi</b></i> understand is that the Wheel, <i>Samsara</i>, can become temporarily clogged. Sometimes people reach a point where, in their current life, they're neither advancing towards <i>Moksha</i>, nor helping anyone to do so, neither being happy or making others happy or helping community in any way. In some cases, they're actively hindering others in such a way that whatever good their lives are producing, it's not being worth it.<br /> <br /> So the <i><b>Euthanatoi</b></i> assume the role of unclogging <i>Samsara</i> by ending this life, so the person can reincarnate again and return to advancement. It can be a bad person that hinders others as well as themselves, but it can also be a patient so ill that continuing life will only bring pointless suffering to all involved, a person whose fate from now is to stop advancement, or any other number of things. The point is the <i><b>system</b></i> of <i>Samsara</i>, its health, so to speak, and if a person's life benefits it, or if cleaning the slate is a better course of action.<br /> <br /> Remember that in all cases, they believe in reincarnation. Actually eliminating the <i>Atma</i>, the real immortal soul, is possibly the most terrible sin, only to be carried if that soul's continued existence is truly anathema to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>While one can see why you used the Vedantist terminology for the most part, the analogy breaks down toward the end as the Gilgul of the Avatar is a concept that does not have a reasonable point of comparison. Conflating the Atma with the Avatar, while pretty explicitly what the authors were going for with Euthanatoi theology, does not work as the Atma is wholly immortal in Vedantist thought, whilst the Avatar can be annihilated. Additionally, there is the problem that assuming that one allowed that to be the case, Brahman would naturally be taken with it in destruction. You did provide a good outline of Euthanatoi ethics, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T19:01:48-07:00","id":1553079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553075#post1553075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While one can see why you used the Vedantist terminology for the most part, the analogy breaks down toward the end as the Gilgul of the Avatar is a concept that does not have a reasonable point of comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware of that, explaining the <b>Euthanatoi</b> really was the focus. And it's a staple of Mage to bend real world religious concepts to apply the in-game facts, it's not as if the <i>Atma</i> is the only concept of a soul that some Tradition identifies with the Avatar despite Gilgul being impossible from their IRL religion's perspective. And the game has two escape clauses to this, anyway: first, Gilgul isn't guaranteed to be eternal (which is something the Order of Hermes worry about from time to time, as they weight the implications). Second, while <u>most</u> Mages conflate the Avatar with the Soul, this isn't universally accepted.<br /> <br /> But yeah, within the Vedas it would be ridiculous to consider the destruction of the <i>Atma</i> even possible, much less necessary at any point whatsoever. And in Hindu thought, it would be a hard thing to conciliate such thought with <i>Brahman</i>. Some of the traditions derived from the <i>Vedas</i>, like some Buddhist schools, would have a somewhat easier time conciliating this idea as <i>Brahman</i> doesn't exactly exist there, but it's still a hell, of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T11:24:22-07:00","id":1553105,"title":"","content":"It's also part of the setting that the revelation that Avatars and souls have evidence of not being the same thing is relatively new to mage society. For most of history, mages didn't even perceive Avatars as separate entities from the self, and the commonality of experience of Avatars exerting independence to the mages they're bonded to didn't really even set in until the Enlightenment era. This was one of the Time of Judgement plot threads as the Revised metaplot accelerated this dissonance between mage and Avatar to the point of representing an existential threat to there being new mages in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T10:51:55-07:00","id":1553141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553011#post1553011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.It has ties to necromancy trough how the underworld and the concept of decay relates to magick (which it's a little contrived, but it's what it is).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this could be its own thread, but Spirit seems more like &quot;the necromancy sphere&quot; to me (especially anything that in VTM would be called &quot;Path of the Sepulchre,&quot; which IRL, would be the most authentic form of necromancy). Calling ghosts? Spirit. Putting down ghosts? Spirit. Asking a ghost to tell you the future? Spirit. Forcing a ghost to spy on someone? Spirit. Instructing a ghost to kill someone? Spirit. <br /> <br /> If you want to get into reanimation, that's either Matter/Prime or Life/Prime, but for a singular sphere that fits necromancy, it would be Spirit. Entropy is only tangentially related to necromancy because it allows you to go directly to the Underworld rather than stepping sideways and then finding a portal, but even then, that feels like it should be a Spirit primary thing, with Entropy maybe added if you want to preserve the feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T11:00:59-07:00","id":1553142,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatoi, or more accurately, the Chakravanti, view themselves as the custodians of the Dharmachakra, or, in Western terms, the custodians of the Wheel of Fate. Thus Entropy is their sphere because it is the sphere that allows you to see or mold fate. To see when someone has strayed from their Dharma, Entropy is the sphere that would likely be used. To put someone back on their path if such a thing is possible, Entropy would also be the sphere that would be used. Entropy could also be used to kill Nephandi or vampires through Entropy 2's bad luck effects and Entropy 4's pattern destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-13T21:37:07-07:00","id":1553161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553141#post1553141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(especially anything that in VTM would be called &quot;Path of the Sepulchre,&quot; which IRL, would be the most authentic form of necromancy)<br /> <br /> If you want to get into reanimation, that's either Matter/Prime or Life/Prime</div> </div> </div> </div>IRL Necromancy wouldn't be like the &quot;Path of the Sepulchre&quot;. It would be more like <b>Entropy</b> and <b>Time</b> divination effects with a Shamanic focus and using either a corpse or a sympathetic connection to a dead person as an Instrument. Actual ghosts showing up is an entirely optional and secondary effect.<br /> <br /> For Reanimation, it would have to include <b>Matter</b>, always. You can't affect a corpse without it. What other Spheres it will require depends entirely on what you want this &quot;animation&quot; to entail.<br /> <br /> Other than that, agreed. In fact, the book itself agrees. While <b>Entropy</b> is frequently associated to the dead because it kills people, targeting actual ghosts with it is actually ill advised, and the only consequence is a <b>very</b> angry ghost, not any sort of real life or fictional necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T08:29:41-07:00","id":1553168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553161#post1553161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than that, agreed. In fact, the book itself agrees. While <b>Entropy</b> is frequently associated to the dead because it kills people, targeting actual ghosts with it is actually ill advised, and the only consequence is a <b>very</b> angry ghost, not any sort of real life or fictional necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's true, there's exactly one and only one mention of Necromancy on M20, and that's as a specialty you can chose for Entropy<br /> <br /> Plus, on top of it being necessary to enter the Underworld (and to some other necromantic shenanigans, such as the Necrosynthesis rotes and the one that protects against Arcanoi, from the Euthanatos tradition book), Entropy magick it's at -2 difficulty on the Underworld (Book of Worlds), it flows easily because it's a realm strongly related to Entropy.<br /> <br /> It's &quot;ill adviced&quot; precisely because it has a lot to do with necromancy, and not the opposite (and necromancy it's &quot;evil&quot;), Entropy it's related to the Underworld and the Shadow because it's related with Oblivion - and that's a very bad thing/force that will twist your intent and cause bad things to happen.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean when I say &quot;It has ties to necromancy trough how the underworld and the concept of decay relates to magick&quot;<br /> <br /> This may seem contrived, as much of what's perceived as pop-culture &quot;necromancer kit&quot; it's tied to other Sphere. If I wanted to make a necromancer I probably wouldn't put more than one dot on Entropy, and take the Merit that allows to enter the underworld with Spirit.<br /> <br /> I DO think it's contrived and forced. But the fact of the matter it's that the books DO want Entropy to be related with necromancy.<br /> <br /> The whole cosmology and a good chunk of WoD metaplot it's built arround the idea of death as a corrupted force, from Oblivion to the Wyrm, to Entropy and necromancy as a concept. And that's probably why it's chugged together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T13:30:56-07:00","id":1553185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553161#post1553161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IRL Necromancy wouldn't be like the &quot;Path of the Sepulchre&quot;. It would be more like <b>Entropy</b> and <b>Time</b> divination effects with a Shamanic focus and using either a corpse or a sympathetic connection to a dead person as an Instrument. Actual ghosts showing up is an entirely optional and secondary effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken. I was more thinking of conjuring a spirit and asking it to tell you the future, rather than just telling the future with a shamanic/necromancy oriented focus, but that works too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For Reanimation, it would have to include <b>Matter</b>, always. You can't affect a corpse without it. What other Spheres it will require depends entirely on what you want this &quot;animation&quot; to entail.<br /> <br /> Other than that, agreed. In fact, the book itself agrees. While <b>Entropy</b> is frequently associated to the dead because it kills people, targeting actual ghosts with it is actually ill advised, and the only consequence is a <b>very</b> angry ghost, not any sort of real life or fictional necromancy. </div> </div> </div>And yet necromancy is an Entropy specialty. Seems like a waste of a specialty to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T21:09:01-07:00","id":1553196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553168#post1553168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I DO think it's contrived and forced. But the fact of the matter it's that the books DO want Entropy to be related with necromancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I stand corrected to the degree that it applies.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't really put almost nothing that one would link to Fantasy Necromancy under <b>Entropy</b>, except as far as it forces its presence just for thematic purposes. The whole shenanigan is complex, weird and contrived, but in the end both things are true: Fantasy Necromancy is mostly <b>Spirit</b> (although not only that), but at the same time the book makes a point of saying that <b>Entropy</b> has everything to do with it.<br /> <br /> Just FYI: I'm referring to Fantasy Necromancy just because we already touched Real Life Necromancy, which is a very particular thing, but the distinction isn't all that relevant for game purposes, nor is it in any way more or less Necromancy for this conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553185#post1553185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet necromancy is an Entropy specialty. Seems like a waste of a specialty to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Although if the ST just plays along with tackling a dot of <b>Entropy</b> at any &quot;necromantic&quot; effect, then it may be worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T18:17:06-07:00","id":1553245,"title":"","content":"Don't really think the Euthanatoi's implied connection to cycles of reincarnation was ever really intended to be linked to their specialty Sphere? It always felt more like nonmechanical flavor or grist for sessions even though rationally a Euthanatos assassin would have an informational magical skillset for actually figuring out who to kill along with the powers for the murder itself. Guessing that Entropy was supposed to pull double duty there with its whole assessing probabilities and divinatory aspect, but it was a bit of a stretch. Kind of surprised they never had a background for it along the lines of Dream or something. Then again it probably would have just served as a point sink for something that was ultimately going to be Storyteller fiat anyway. <br /> <br /> Everything that all of you said about Spirit and necromancy was pretty spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-17T19:53:02-07:00","id":1553247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1553010-the-euthanatos-tradition-and-the-sphere-of-entropy?p=1553245#post1553245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't really think the Euthanatoi's implied connection to cycles of reincarnation was ever really intended to be linked to their specialty Sphere?</div> </div> </div> </div>From their own POV, probably not, especially as editions went on.<br /> <br /> But while the rules used to reinforce them through price cuts in XP, the specialty Spheres exist primarily within the setting as the Seats in the Council of Nine, which is a social/metaphysical construct.<br /> <br /> So, while this construct isn't strictly Chakravanti, but mostly derived from Hermetic thought, there's still a mystical reason for them to be linked to <b>Entropy</b>, however any particular member feels about this reason (or the link itself).<br /> <br /> They're first and foremost linked to <b>Entropy</b> because they were made by the devs to represent <b>Entropy</b>, so there is at least a thematic link in the first place, not a practical one. Then there's a lot of aspects of the game and the setting that reinforce the concept of each Tradition being intrinsically linked to their Sphere, despite M20 deviating in how strong it presents this link (it used to be a huger thing).<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it is both artificial and metaphysical. No Tradition has to be constrained to a given Sphere, and in fact none was when they came up. It is both an imposition from the rules (for a Specialty Sphere) and from the Council of Nine (as an institution within it). Yet, it is in a way present in them since always, both as their Doylist <i>raison d'\u00eatre</i> since inception, and interpretation of some defining aspect of them that justified them being chosen for that Seat. It is a mystical position they assumed based on their identity, and Mage being Mage, the distinction between symbol and symbolized is blurred at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}